WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.800
Have you ever wondered what actually happens when you type a website into your browser?

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.533
First, your browser asks the internet where that website lives.

3
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:17.000
A system called DNS translates the website name into an IP address.

4
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.033
Your browser sends a request to a server at that IP address.

5
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:26.867
The server responds with files — HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

6
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:31.600
HTML creates the structure — the skeleton of every page.

7
00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:36.933
CSS controls how everything looks — colors, fonts, layout, and spacing.

8
00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:42.467
JavaScript brings the page to life — making it interactive and responsive.

9
00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:48.800
Your browser combines all three files and renders the page you see on screen.

10
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.733
Every modern website goes through this exact process in milliseconds.

11
00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:58.900
Frontend developers design and build these web experiences every day.

12
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.800
